cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vibe-sentinel in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: vibe-sentinel
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"
abstract: >
  Safeguards a codebase against the problems AI coding agents introduce:
  structural drift, secrets at rest, unvetted dependencies, and dangerous
  commands. Probes measure the shape of a tree — modules per package,
  commentary against code, where a pattern occurs, the installed version and
  origin of every dependency — and every run is recorded to an append-only
  history that later runs compare against, over a horizon and as a fitted
  direction as well as against a baseline. Lenses put a question about what
  moved to the model, in the project's own words. Gates report a standing
  state instead of a transition — a key at rest, where a dependency came
  from, what licence arrived with it — on every run, cleared only by a pin
  that records a reason and a date. An optional PreToolUse hook journals a
  coding agent's commands and reviews a dangerous one against what that
  agent already ran; it is the only check that can refuse an action, and it
  ships off by default. Runs entirely on the user's machine via a local
  OpenAI-compatible model, which is required.
authors:
